# Keep development-only material out of `git archive` output — which is
# what GitHub's branch and release downloads are, and therefore what
# `update.py --dev` installs on a beta tester's machine. They need the
# application, not the suite that tests it.
#
# This applies to release archives cut from main as well, and that is the
# point: main keeps tests/ so CI can actually verify a release snapshot,
# while the zip an analyst downloads still doesn't carry them. The branch
# needs the suite; the artifact does not.
#
# Deliberately NOT applied to docs/ or .github/: a downloaded tree that
# can't tell you how it's meant to work is a worse artifact than a
# slightly larger one.
.claude/            export-ignore
scripts/release.py   export-ignore
tests/test_release_script.py export-ignore
tests/               export-ignore
bench/               export-ignore
CLAUDE.md            export-ignore
requirements-dev.txt export-ignore
